# The Analytics Agent serves HTTPS with a SELF-SIGNED cert (CN=localhost.localdomain).
# Node's fetch rejects it by default, which chat.service reports as the generic
# "assistant is unavailable". Trusting this one cert keeps verification ON for
# every other TLS call — do NOT reach for NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 here.
# Re-export with: openssl s_client -connect <agent-host>:8001 | openssl x509 > certs/agent.pem
# NOTE: Node reads this at process START, so dotenv loading .env is too late — it
# only works because b2b.service pulls this file in via EnvironmentFile. Running
# the server by hand needs it on the command line: NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=... node ...
NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS="/opt/B2B-Site/server/certs/agent.pem"
